# =====================================================================
# Build context exclusions
# =====================================================================
# Without this file, `docker build` sends the ENTIRE project directory to the
# Docker daemon on every build. That is slow, and it breaks outright on any
# broken symlink in the tree — which is exactly what happened here:
#
#   failed to solve: invalid file request backend/public/storage
#
# `backend/public/storage` is created by `php artisan storage:link` inside the
# container. It is an absolute symlink to /var/www/html/storage/app/public, a
# path that only exists inside the container. On Windows it dangles, and the
# daemon cannot tar a dangling link.
#
# Both problems are solved by excluding these paths from the context. They are
# all generated — either by the container at runtime, or by the Dockerfile
# itself — so nothing here needs to be copied in.
# =====================================================================

# --- Container-generated runtime state ---------------------------------
# Written by `storage:link`, the scheduler, and the queue worker.
backend/public/storage
backend/storage

# Cache and discovery manifests, rebuilt during the image build.
backend/bootstrap/cache

# Compiled SPA. The Dockerfile builds this fresh in the `assets` stage.
backend/public/build

# --- Host-side dependency trees ----------------------------------------
# The Dockerfile runs `composer install` and `npm ci` itself. Shipping the
# host's copies would shadow the container's and can differ by platform.
backend/vendor
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist

# --- Local configuration and secrets -----------------------------------
# Environment is supplied by docker-compose.yml / the host, never baked in.
.env
backend/.env
*.key

# --- Version control and tooling ---------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.swp

# --- Logs and editor noise ---------------------------------------------
*.log
backend/storage/logs/*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Docs and scripts not needed at runtime ----------------------------
docs
*.md
!README.md
